L000270	\emph{Videos.--} We also produced videos of the density fluctuations from CCD shown in the right panels of Fig.~\ref{fig:48Ca}. The videos start at time $t=0$ and end at time $t=t_{\rm max}=200$~fm$/c$.
L000271	We see that the amplitudes of the fluctuations are particularly large at the beginning (because we start from the Hartree-Fock density) and later become smaller.  For this reason, we choose the starting point for the calculation of the time-averaged density to be $\tau_{\rm min}=100$~fm$/c$.
